cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Chip-aware placement for QAOA on modular quantum devices (simulation study)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chenchupradeep"
    given-names: "Degala"
    affiliation: "SRM University AP"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pradeepdegalaroyal/modular-chip-aware-qaoa-placement"
abstract: "On modular quantum processors, chip-to-chip coupler gates are much noisier than intra-chip gates, and QAOA's cost layer puts one two-qubit gate on every graph edge, so the vertex-to-chip assignment decides how many noisy gates the circuit contains. This simulation study (n = 8-12 qubits, two chips, Pauli-trajectory noise) measures how much MaxCut approximation ratio (AR) a chip-aware placement (Kernighan-Lin bisection) recovers compared with a chip-oblivious random placement. At a 20x coupler/intra-chip error ratio it gains 0.04-0.06 AR on average for both community-structured and 3-regular graphs, and it gains exactly nothing when the ratio is 1."
keywords:
  - QAOA
  - modular quantum processors
  - qubit placement
  - Kernighan-Lin
  - noise simulation
  - MaxCut
